# NetIRC Defender V3 — regexp_akill.conf
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to datadir as regexp_akill.conf (see defender.conf: datadir=).
# One rule per line:  <Perl regex>	<reason text>
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. Match is case-insensitive
# against:  nick!ident@host realname  (single line built at sign-on; see regexp_akill.pm).
# Prefer short patterns; heavy regexes are time-limited (regexp_akill_alarm_sec).
# You can also manage rules live: regexp_akill add / del / list on the control channel.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Example (uncomment to use — tune to your network; wrong patterns cause false G-lines):
#^evil!~?bad\@123\.456\..*	Automated sign-on pattern (example)
